gin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-style:italic">What, realistically, could =
a Democrat-led Congress do to restrain Trump=3F =E2=80=94 </span><span>Keit=
h Parr, France</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;co=
lor:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Annie Karni, cong=
ressional correspondent:</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgi=
a,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>If Democrats win back the House =
=E2=80=94 the lower chamber of Congress =E2=80=94 they will have subpoena p=
ower and will be conducting oversight and investigations into the administr=
ation. And they will have to consider whether it is worth their time and th=
e political price that may come with moving forward with impeachment agains=
t cabinet officials, or the president himself. If they win back the Senate =
=E2=80=94 the upper chamber =E2=80=94 Democrats would also have the power t=
o block any Trump cabinet appointments or judicial nominees.</span></p><p s=
tyle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><sp=
an>They will also be in control of what bills come to the floor. And many D=
emocrats think that some of the popular legislation they plan to bring up i=
f they win the majority =E2=80=94 like reinstating subsidies for people who=
 buy the health insurance known as Obamacare =E2=80=94 could </span><a href=
=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter/NH_bAWoEfbEMMB9gjAZsTQ~~/AAAAARA~/3=
lBD74KSfpe5wN8EQz-gbGbVMu1o6VIld-xHgy9XavPHkuaT3NbblOBMUihu30j6glfcOQGgAu7k=
